***********************************************
   Example fep calculations for PhX -> PhY  
***********************************************

FEP calculations are setup to allow computation of relative free
energies of hydration for substituted benzenes. The following FEPs           
are included:

 CH2OMe <- Pr    NH2 <- NHMe <- NMe2 <- NO2 <- COMe -> CONH2
           !      !                             !
    iPr -> Et -> Me -> H <- F <- Cl <- Br     MeC=CH2
           !      !         !     !
F <- OH <- OMe   CF3        CN    H
   / !     !
 SH  NH2   SMe

The Z-matrices illustrate the setup for standard FEP transformations.
The same Z-matrices are used for the gas-phase and aqueous calculations
in the gas and aq directories. 

For example, ch3-cf3 is for PhCH3 -> PhCF3.
The Z-matrix for the FEP calculation is called ch3-cf3.z
It uses OPLS-AA parameters with fully flexible geometries.

Run the gas-phase calculation:
xFEPGAS ch3-cf3
The resulting total deltaG is dGgas in ch3-cf3.gas/sumout:
 Sum of DeltaGs =   10.00    
 Sigma          =    0.00

Run the aqueous-phase calculation:
xFEPAQ ch3-cf3
The resulting total deltaG is dGaq in ch3-cf3.aq/sumout:
 Sum of DeltaGs =   11.36       
 Sigma          =    0.08     


The thermodynamic cycle is

               dGgas
     PhCH3    ------>     PhCF3
       I                    I
       I                    I
       I dG(PhCH3)          I dG(PhCF3)
       I                    I
       V                    V
     PhCH3    ------>     PhCF3
               dGaq

  deltaG hydration =
     dG(PhCF3) - dG(PhCH3) = dGaq - dGgas
                           = 11.36 - 10.00
			   = 1.36  (exptl = 0.64)

Execution times on a 2.8 GHz Pentium:
gas phase         20 minutes
aqueous phase      6 hours  

Directories aq10 and gas10 contain the input   for the FEP calculations
using 10 windows. The input files using 25 windows are in aq25 and gas25.
---------------------------------------------------------------------

To run on the Yale queuing system
xFEPAQQ ch3-cf3

All of the FEP calculations in water have been run simultaneously
by listing the Z-matrix names (with the .z) in "filenames", then
in the aq directory
xMANY filenames xFEPAQQ

and in the gas directory
xMANY filenames xFEPGAS
(the gas jobs could be run on the queue too, but they are
much faster and can be run sequentially)

The results have been collected in the Excel file PhXtoY.xls
